From: Harvi654 <202698022+Harvi654@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] combase: Look up per-user in-process classes.

AI-assisted (Codex), original code; LGPL-2.1-or-later. Not submitted upstream.

Non-elevated Windows 10 selected the user registration over the machine
registration when both named the same in-process class. It also resolved
the per-user ProgID and TreatAs keys. Search the current user's classes
before the existing machine lookup for those reads. Keep explicit registry
view selection and preserve other HKCR callers.

v2 (2026-11-24): The native Windows 10 fixture found that High integrity
callers cannot activate a class registered only in HKCU. Use the thread
token when impersonating and otherwise the process token. At High or
above, or if integrity cannot be determined, use the existing machine
lookup. This revision requires the server and ntdll token integrity
patches so a limited Wine process reports its actual integrity level.

v3 2026-11-25: no code change. The combase test moves from tests-first
into the patch; the six todo_wine/todo_wine_if marks on checks this
patch passes are dropped (CoGetClassObject, CoCreateInstance, the
server marker, CLSIDFromProgID, ProgIDFromCLSID, CoGetTreatAsClass).
Promoted to the series for winum-11.22-3.

